# Staged patches must keep LF line endings in every checkout. With
# core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) a .patch is otherwise written as
# CRLF, its blank context lines become "\r", and `git apply` rejects the file
# as "corrupt patch" before reading a hunk; --ignore-whitespace does not help,
# because the failure is a parse error, not a whitespace mismatch.
proposals/*.patch text eol=lf

# The KNOWN-LIMITS pin's body-sha256 is taken over the file's bytes with no
# line-ending fold, so a CRLF checkout digests differently from the LF bytes
# git stores and the committed-pin tripwire fails on Windows (limit 81).
KNOWN-LIMITS.md text eol=lf
